\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {End-to-End System Architecture and Dataflow of the Two-Tier Hybrid Cascade Physics-RAG Framework.} \textbf  {(1)} Natural language operational queries are decoupled by the Hybrid Query Parser into structured columnar SQL predicates and a 14D target physical invariant vector $\mathbf  {z}_{\text  {target}}$. \textbf  {(2)} Tier\nobreakspace  {}1 executes sub-15-millisecond zero-copy predicate pushdown over columnar Parquet storage via DuckDB, pruning the multi-site golden window archive ($N = 175{,}392$ records) into an anchored spatiotemporal candidate subset $\mathcal  {C}_{\text  {filtered}}$, eliminating cross-decadal manifold degeneracy. \textbf  {(3)} Tier\nobreakspace  {}2 projects candidates into the 14D Buckingham $\pi $ invariant latent space, evaluating them via an asymmetric Directional Pareto ranking objective (Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\ref {eq:directional_pareto}) that penalizes sub-threshold calm states and rewards kinetic disequilibrium excess, eliminating chronological blindness and synchronizing to true hydrodynamic storm apexes ($t^*$). \textbf  {(4)} Top-$k$ target event timestamps trigger zero-copy pointer retrieval to hydrate continuous antecedent parent sequences ($\mathbf  {X}_{\text  {parent}} \in \mathbb  {R}^{145 \times 14}$, $\pm 72\text  { hours}$), capturing multi-channel wave steepening, the $26.5\times $ kinetic surge in $\Upsilon $, and Total Water Level confronting berm crests ($Z_{\text  {crest}}$), eliminating Markovian memorylessness. \textbf  {(5)} Retrieved states are evaluated by the Conformal Quantile Regressor, injecting certified prediction intervals $[c_{\text  {lo}}, c_{\text  {hi}}]$ and hydrograph volatility states into downstream LLM reasoning engines.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:physics_rag_architecture}{{2}{5}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Four-Panel 2D UMAP Projection of the 14D Invariant Latent Space ($N = 12{,}000$ Stratified Records).} \textbf  {(a)} Morphodynamic state continuum colored by Dean number $\Omega $, displaying a continuous chromatic gradient from reflective steep profiles ($\Omega < 1$) to dissipative flat states ($\Omega > 7$). \textbf  {(b)} Hydrodynamic kinetic energy continuum $\log _{10}\Upsilon $, showing baseline calm records clustering near the manifold core while extreme storm work projects into outer peripheral filaments. \textbf  {(c)} Breaker dissipation regimes classified by Iribarren number $\xi $, showing topological separation between spilling ($\xi < 0.5$, cyan) and plunging ($\xi \ge 0.5$, pink) wave dissipation. \textbf  {(d)} Universal cross-site invariance: records from all four global observatories (Duck, Narrabeen, Torrey Pines, Truc Vert) interleave across identical topological branches, confirming cross-site physical similitude.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:umap_4panel}{{3}{5}}
\newlabel{eq:directional_pareto}{{16}{5}}
